  "summary": "The generated code is a clean, well-structured TypeScript implementation of Key Vault secret CRUD operations. It correctly uses all required SDK methods (setSecret, getSecret, beginDeleteSecret, purgeDeletedSecret), properly awaits the LRO poller before purging, and follows async/await patterns throughout. The main gaps are: (1) no RestError-specific error handling — only generic Error is caught, (2) no use of @azure/logger for SDK diagnostic logging, and (3) the general error handling lacks retries/timeouts. These are the only 4 failures out of 20 criteria.",
